    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok thanks. i tried to peek under there but it's really dark and cramped. is there a specific way i should dry it out? like should i just use a towel or do i need to tip the whole thing out to get the water from the bottom tray out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Tipping the whole dishwasher out is generally not recommended unless you are prepared for a major spill, which is probably more trouble than it's worth. You can try to get a good view and dry the area using a shop vac or a highly absorbent cloth, like a microfiber towel, which you can gently press into the crevices. If the water is pooled in the bottom tray area, try to carefully reach in with a flashlight and wick up as much as you can with a towel. Remember, the goal is to make sure the sensor and the surrounding area are completely dry before the machine can operate normally.",
